      "note": "runtime device control for Claude/Codex only -- hermesProfiles [] because hermes carries native Home Assistant runtime tools, so the skill would be redundant there; the authoring companion is the separate npx-tracked home-assistant-best-practices"
    },
    "sql-toolkit": {
      "slug": "@gitgoodordietrying/sql-toolkit",
      "registry": "https://clawhub.ai",
      "note": "was hermes-hub-owned in nicodemus (hermesRegistry); now clawhub-updates in the store and reaches nicodemus via a store symlink -- the retired hub install is unowned live state to hand-remove"
    },
    "summarize-pro": {
      "slug": "@mkpareek0315/summarize-pro",
      "registry": "https://clawhub.ai",
      "note": "was hermes-hub-owned in default (hermesRegistry) and a HERMES_COLLISION_NAMES entry; the hub install was its ONLY hermes copy (no catalog copy wins the name, exactly like todoist-cli), so it now reaches default via a store symlink -- the retired hub install is unowned live state to hand-remove. Store install+update round-trip verified live 2026-07-09"
    }
